{
  "$comment": "The quote before a run of the seven steps whose run measures the file it is given — Video SFX, Video Mask, Video Depth, Pitch & Tempo, Dubbing, and Video Upscale on each of its two measuring models (`topaz`, and `nodaroUpscale`, the per-second model) — read by BOTH estimates over the same graphs through the one measured walk (`measuredWireLengthSec`, @nodaro/render-rules) with each step's slack (`MEASURED_INPUT_PLANNED_CLIP_SLACK_SEC`: 0.1 s on each clip a node makes for the five that measure the container, one 24 fps frame for both Video Upscale steps: one hold counts the video stream's frames, the other bills the clip's seconds rounded up, so any slack under a second is the same figure there): the editor's (frontend getModelIdentifier for the row steps, PRICING_UNIT_ESTIMATORS for Dubbing and both Video Upscale providers — the node's pill, its Run button, the confirm and the workflow badge) and the server's workflow estimate (CreditsService.estimateWorkflowCreditsAt, the step's own line). Each case wires its sources into the step `c`; an edge with no `target` goes into `c` on the step's input (`@input`: `video`, Pitch & Tempo's `in`; `handles` overrides it). `steps` limits a case to some steps (default every step but `lipSync`, a Lip Sync priced by the seconds of its audio, which only the cases that list it name; its figure is the billed seconds, `null` a length nothing knows before the run: the server quotes the most a run takes, the editor a 15 s estimate marked ≈). Expected figures: the row's seconds for Video SFX (`replicate-mmaudio:<N>s`), Video Mask (`<provider>-video:<N>s`) and Video Depth (`video-depth-anything:<N>s`); the started minutes for Pitch & Tempo (`pitch-tempo:<N>m`) and Dubbing (target `es`); the Topaz units (a 1080p target, 30 fps, a 16:9 frame); the seconds `nodaroUpscale` bills (at least 1): 0 for a clip the graph KNOWS is past its 60-second limit (an upload, a measured Library clip, a take's record — the run refuses it before anything is held, and no estimate prices it), and the 60 seconds a run bills at most for a PLANNED length past it, which is an upper bound and no proof the run refuses it. An input whose length nothing can tell before the run is quoted at the step's cap for Video SFX, Video Mask, Video Depth and Pitch & Tempo, and at a minimum for Dubbing (1 minute) and both Video Upscale providers (a 10-second clip) — those runs measure their input and are charged its real length. `whole` = a whole run (the editor's whole-run set, the server with no run set); `alone` = the step's own Run and its pill (editor) and a run of `c` alone (server); `partial` = exactly that run set on both sides.",
